WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.802
-And finally,
two weeks ago,

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.937
a series of
group-chat messages

00:00:04.937 --> 00:00:06.706
sent by the governor
of Puerto Rico

00:00:06.706 --> 00:00:08.641
and his advisers
leaked to the press.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.477
It contained misogynist
and homophobic comments

00:00:11.477 --> 00:00:13.112
in a conversation
where the group laughed

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:15.015
about victims of
Hurricane Maria.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.682
After years of
political corruption,

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:17.684
it was the last straw,

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:19.218
so Puerto Ricans
took to the streets

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:20.720
to demand the governor's
resignation.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.221
One of our writers,
Jenny Hagel,

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:24.657
is Puerto Rican,
and she's here to comment.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:28.828
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.362
-Thanks, Seth.

00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:32.531
Earlier this month,
Puerto Ricans obtained evidence

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:34.466
that their leader
was corrupt and immoral.

00:00:34.466 --> 00:00:35.868
So, what did they do?

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:37.570
Wait two years
for Robert Mueller

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.705
to write the world's longest
book report?

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:42.709
No. They took matters
into their own hands.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.610
They staged
a two-week-long protest

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.178
demanding that
the governor resign,

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.648
and they made the whole thing
look like a giant party.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:49.682
Take a look.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:55.154 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:55.154 --> 00:01:00.627 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.828
That's a political protest.

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:05.565
That looked for fun
than most weddings.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.135
Plus, it's not every day
you get to see someone

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.404
fight injustice
with a cowbell.

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.472
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:13.706
Everyone was out
in the streets --

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.543
young people, old people,
even Spiderman.

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:25.051
Or, as he's known in
Puerto Rico, Pedro Parker.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.352
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.021
Protesters played instruments
in the streets,

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:30.422
and people who didn't
have instruments

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:32.024
banged pots and pans.

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:34.961
Watch this woman stand up to
a group of police officers

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.329
in riot gear.

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.233
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:43.970
We're over here
on the mainland going,

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.906
"The new is so overwhelming.
What can I do?"

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:49.375
And this woman's like,
"Do you have a pot?"

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:50.943
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:52.512
"Bang it."

00:01:52.512 --> 00:01:53.680
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.814
Yeah.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.549
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.220
These demonstrations brought out
the best in everyone.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.556
10 years ago,
Ricky Martin was in the closet.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.625
Last week, he was in the middle
of that protest,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:10.029
on top of a truck,
waving this flag.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:13.399
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.035
It's like he's performing in
a way more fun revival

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.337
of "Les Mis."

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.771
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.506
By the way,
it's not a coincidence

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:21.907
that Ricky Martin
was there.

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:24.510
In those leaked text messages,
a government official

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.278
made a homophobic joke
about him.

00:02:26.278 --> 00:02:28.747
Imagine insulting a celebrity
on a text chain

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:31.851
with your friends, and then,
that celebrity comes for you

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:32.985
in real life.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:35.154
That's terrifying.

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.890
That's like if you said you
didn't like the season finale

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.092
of "Big Little Lies,"
and then, suddenly,

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.194
Meryl Streep was
outside your window.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.863
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:47.600
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.802
But here's the thing about the
demonstrations in Puerto Rico --

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.737
They weren't just cool.
They worked.

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.872
After two weeks,
the governor resigned.

00:02:53.872 --> 00:02:56.142
Puerto Ricans got their
corrupt leader out of office

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:57.810
in two weeks.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.245
We've had
two and a half years,

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:01.247
and we can't get ours
off Twitter.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.616
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:06.819
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.956
Donald Trump thinks
Puerto Ricans aren't Americans.

00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:13.893
Well, last week, they were
the best example of Americans.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.695
They exercised their rights to
free speech and free assembly,

00:03:16.695 --> 00:03:19.765
and they peacefully protested
wrong until they made it right.

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:23.202
Plus, they avenged
Ricky Martin.

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:25.003
So, let's follow their example.

00:03:25.003 --> 00:03:26.072
Call you representatives.

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.973
Volunteer. Canvass. Protest.

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:30.709
And if that seems like
too much, do you have a pot?

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:31.777
Bang it.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:34.313
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:37.917
-Jenny Hagel, everybody.

